# Incident Report 004 — FSRM Management Console Crash and Inconsistent Quota Enumeration

**Project:** Active Directory Home Lab  
**Environment:** Windows Server 2022 | VMware Workstation Pro  
**Domain:** Turtle.local  
**Incident Type:** Windows Server Management Interface Failure  
**Severity:** Moderate — Isolated Lab Environment  
**Status:** Resolved  
**Root Cause:** Undetermined — Temporary management-component issue suspected

---

## 1. Executive Summary

While learning to configure storage quotas using File Server Resource Manager (FSRM), I encountered two unexpected management problems.

First, the FSRM Microsoft Management Console (MMC) snap-in generated exceptions and crashed when I attempted to configure notification thresholds.

Second, PowerShell commands intended to retrieve existing FSRM quotas returned no objects, even though the quotas were visible in the graphical console.

Investigation confirmed that the FSRM service was running and that its native `dirquota` command-line utility could successfully enumerate and modify quotas.

After installing VMware Tools and restarting the Windows Server 2022 virtual machine, both management interfaces began functioning normally.

The precise cause of the original failures was not established.

